{"title":"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The numeral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21383a2b05dbe4ed4ecd095273f0cabc32b78a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> in base a represents the same number as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/90100e7ec57be3145070551137e9c47224adb4d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$74$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Assuming that both bases are positive \nintegers, the least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> written as a Roman numeral, is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e9092a6fa9a9f7ccdd522e1daec8b7aaa267069.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\mathrm{XIII}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\mathrm{XV}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\mathrm{XXI}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\mathrm{XXIV}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\mathrm{XVI}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"485\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/80657b7404f8d2eda64b1c68bae18e87c5ef0603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a+7=7b+4\\implies 7b=4a+3\\implies b=\\frac{4a+3}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"397\" height=\"37\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e994ef8356294bf679460dac92b14e7caa66cb91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a+3\\equiv 0\\implies 4a\\equiv 4\\implies a\\equiv1 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"18\" />. The smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/2223410f9bb64127d5fd1518e51311b25a152c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{4\\cdot8+3}{7}=\\frac{35}{7}=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"178\" height=\"37\" />. However, the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is not valid in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we have to try a larger value. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7c192903ca3a1fa8fb98064fbd1fa2011a62ab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=8+7=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"14\" />, gives a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511442c412d779c127a85292708099b5c9927951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15*4+3}{7}=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"112\" height=\"37\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, which is valid. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/36931d225d68ee0c017c2fbb6bbef83bf41bca36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15+9=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22e3c0c8c8f8193e0b8bb1533c076ff5fbe4c7a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{XXIV}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> as a roman numeral, and thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5c1377bf6aba7b33447be49ea1d3822630e07be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\mathrm{XXIV}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"102\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME\" title=\"1971 AHSME\">1971 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1971 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1971\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=